# Capacity model and pilot roadmap. Inputs are copied, versioned model outputs.
scale=json.loads((ROOT/'src/scale-data.json').read_text());pilot=json.loads((ROOT/'src/pilot-actions.json').read_text());peak=next(s for s in scale['scenarios'] if s['id']=='100m_peak');sizing=scale['storage'][-1]
scale_prompt='''Use the published capacity model as an explicit hypothesis, never as a database benchmark. Target 50M parties, 100M relationships and the supplied typed child-table distribution. Normal workload is 10k reads/s + 1k writes/s; design peak is 30k reads/s + 5k writes/s globally. Preserve geography, entitlement, purpose and explicit-deny semantics. Use the scale/ scripts and measured workload aggregates to replace assumptions. The v3 runtime remains a PoC with full scans and a process lock; no optimized production data path has been implemented.\n\n'''
lab='https://sovereign-data-monitor.paulcull.chatgpt.site/scale.html'
add('performance-scale','Engineer for the work. Budget for the tails.','Scale assessment / Edition 06','50 million parties, 100 million relationships, explicit p95/p99 targets and reproducible capacity scenarios.',
'<div class="link-grid"><a href="'+lab+'"><span>INTERACTIVE CAPACITY LAB</span><h3>Explore the scenarios →</h3><p>Regional latency, overload, retention, fanout and recovery.</p></a><a href="'+lab+'#pilot"><span>GATED DELIVERY PLAN</span><h3>Open the pilot backlog →</h3><p>24 actions with owners, dependencies and exit evidence.</p></a><a href="https://sovereign-data-monitor.paulcull.chatgpt.site/scale/scale-and-pilot.md"><span>REPRODUCIBLE ASSESSMENT</span><h3>Read the full model →</h3><p>Methods, assumptions, exact outputs and engineering guidance.</p></a></div>'+
call('Targets and simulations are not achieved database performance',f'This assessment analytically represents the full population and simulates {scale["method"]["foreground_events"]:,} foreground requests plus {scale["method"]["background_events"]:,} background events. It does not load a 100M-row CockroachDB database. A small actual OPA HTTP microbenchmark is reported separately.')+
section('Targets to validate in the pilot',table(['Operation','p95 target','p99 target','Measurement boundary'],[[t['name'],str(t['p95_ms'])+' ms',str(t['p99_ms'])+' ms',t['boundary']] for t in scale['assumptions']['targets']]))+
section('The target workload is an assumption',table(['Dimension','Planning value'],[['Cardinality','50M parties / 100M relationships / 125M participation edges.'],['Normal workload','10k reads + 1k business writes per second, globally.'],['Design peak','30k reads + 5k business writes per second; SG 45%, UK 40%, US 15%.'],['Read shape','Indexed key lookup or bounded view: ≤50 rows / 32KiB. Large portfolios, history scans and search are separate workloads.'],['Sharing','0.8 remote relationship copies on average; minimal party identity to two other physical stores where permitted.'],['Admission','≤60% of measured limiting capacity at design peak if peak must survive loss of an AZ.'],['Hardware','Limited pilot: 3 nodes/region across 3 AZs. Full-scale rehearsal candidate: SG 9 / UK 9 / US 6 nodes, 16 vCPU + 64GiB + 2TB each; not a verified sizing recommendation.']]))+
section('The tail grows when queues stop draining','<img src="capacity-results.png" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px" alt="Capacity model charts for latency saturation, logical storage, outage recovery and replication bandwidth.">'+table(['Selected scenario','SG relationship p99','Maximum DB demand / capacity','Interpretation'],[[s['name'],str(round(next(m['p99_ms'] for m in s['metrics'] if m['region']=='SG' and m['operation']=='relationship_read')))+' ms',f'{s["max_db_demand_ratio"]:.2f}×','Stable in model' if s['stable'] else 'Finite overloaded queue; not sustainable'] for s in scale['scenarios'] if s['id'] in ['100m_peak','100m_125','100m_cold','100m_hotkey','100m_skew','100m_az_loss','100m_headroom','100m_wan']]))+
call('Reserve capacity; do not buy directly from synthetic slot counts','Peak demand is around 88% of the initial assumed DB capacity. A 25% workload increase overloads it. A 50% increase in effective capacity lowers peak demand to about 59%, providing a useful AZ-loss reserve. Effective queue slots are not CPUs. Measure the actual limiting resource, then tune or scale the physical deployment.')+
section('Scale changes the integration design',table(['PoC behavior','Pilot/scale change','Reason'],[['Load full owner graph per command/read','Indexed repositories and bounded reads','Dataset size must not enter per-request complexity.'],['Global process lock','Local serializable transactions, per-resource versions, idempotency and bounded retry','Parallelize unrelated parties without weakening business invariants.'],['Rewrite controls across many scopes','Resource/table authority epochs + dependency work queue','One party or table restriction cannot require a massive foreground transaction.'],['Replace entire projection graph','Versioned deltas with atomic parent closure and manifest/inbox update','Avoid repeated indexes, payload and WAN amplification.'],['Duplicate shared party/contact payload by relationship','Canonical resource payload per permitted physical scope with recipient-context checks','Deduplicate bytes without combining entitlements.'],['Check remote home authority on every read','Strict WAN budget OR approved bounded local authority lease','Low local latency and immediate cross-WAN consistency are different contracts.'],['One poller / raw UI snapshot','Partitioned regional relay, priority revocation, materialized aggregates','Bound queue age, retry storms and monitor load.']]))+
section('Storage is dominated by children and retention',table(['Central case across three regions','Modeled size'],[['Source business rows',f'{sizing["source_rows"]/1e9:.2f} billion'],['Logical incl. projections, controls and 7-day audit',f'{sizing["logical_tb"]:.2f} TB'],['Used after 1.7× indexes, 1.35× KV, 1.25× MVCC, RF=3',f'{sizing["replicated_used_tb"]:.1f} TB'],['Provisioned at 60% fill',f'{sizing["provisioned_tb"]:.1f} TB'],['Audit archive per year before compression/redundancy',f'{sizing["audit_annual_archive_tb"]:.1f} TB']]))+
section('Remote authority needs a deliberate contract','<p>The illustrative synchronous WAN case adds a 180ms median round trip and takes relationship p99 to roughly 309ms. A local-read target requires local facts and an approved freshness contract. The proposed alternative uses resource/scope/table epochs plus a maximum five-second authority lease inclusive of clock tolerance. A partition lease must bind a contiguous applied revocation watermark: a heartbeat alone cannot prove no revocation was missed. Refresh active partitions in batches, not every one of 100M scopes every five seconds. This is a proposed pilot design requiring approval; the current PoC still consults source authority.</p><p>Priority revocation traffic must stay separate from data backfill. A 30-minute UK receiver outage generates about 4.97M pending jobs in the model. At 1.5× incoming-rate service capacity, recovery takes 60 minutes while new traffic continues. If the destination remains unavailable, show purge pending; do not promise completed deletion.</p>')+
section('Method and limits','<p>Sixteen scenarios × three seeds; 360,000 foreground arrivals per run and separate import arrivals. At design peak each run covers roughly ten seconds. This is a finite event model; overload results are growing queues, not steady-state percentiles. Service times, cache misses, retry rates and effective concurrency are assumed. The p99 range across seeds describes random variation, not calibration confidence. Lower population points reuse the same full-scale model capacity and proportionately lower traffic. Real SQL, disk, compaction, fault and long-soak tests remain necessary.</p><p>Targets apply by operation/cell/entity to bounded responses, alongside timeout and error rates. Count dropped load-generator iterations and censored timeouts; do not report successful-only percentiles. The actual OPA microbenchmark measured sequential loopback HTTP only and is not a system throughput benchmark.</p>')+
section('Primary engineering references',sources([('CockroachDB production topology, memory and storage','https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/recommended-production-settings'),('SQL performance and query design','https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/performance-best-practices-overview'),('Connection pooling','https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/connection-pooling'),('OPA policy performance','https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/policy-performance'),('Open-arrival load testing and coordinated omission','https://grafana.com/docs/k6/latest/using-k6/scenarios/concepts/open-vs-closed/')])),
scale_prompt+'Build the pilot benchmark, not a benchmark-shaped demo. Generate full indexed child-table cardinality with reproducible degree and policy skew. Use an open arrival model; 60-minute design-peak test and 24-hour normal soak. Report p95/p99/p99.9 per operation and region, errors, dropped iterations, DB resource use, retries, oldest revocation and destination freshness. Replace assumed queue capacity with observations before recommending hardware. Test hot keys, cold caches, background compaction, backup and an AZ loss.')
add('pilot-plan','Prove correctness. Then earn the scale.','PoC to pilot / Edition 06','A gated backlog with named ownership, dependencies and measurable exit evidence.',
call('Planning estimate, not a delivery commitment','An indicative 12–14 week path assumes an experienced cross-functional team, available infrastructure and timely approvals. Start with approved 100k parties / 200k relationships and one business workflow. The 50M/100M performance rehearsal is a separate synthetic-data exercise. The items below are proposed work, not completed controls.')+
section('Sequence the risk reduction',flow([('Decide · weeks 1–2','Approve field footprint, traffic, authority freshness and pilot scope.'),('Foundation · weeks 2–5','Regional HA, identity, indexed access and common local transactions.'),('Correctness · weeks 4–8','Epochs, durable delivery, safe deltas, audit and purge.'),('Prove · weeks 6–11','Full-scale synthetic data, open-load tests, fault and migration rehearsals.'),('Pilot · weeks 12–14+','Read-only shadow, one workflow canary, measured go/no-go.')]))+
section('The action list',table(['ID / priority','Owner','Action','Dependencies','Exit evidence'],[[a['id']+' / '+a['priority'],a['owner'],a['action'],a['dependency'],a['exit']] for a in pilot]))+
section('Pilot exit criteria',table(['Gate','Required evidence'],[['Residency and entitlement','No unauthorised payload or customer-linked metadata in excluded stores, queues, logs or restore targets.'],['Business integrity','Atomic business/hook rollback, idempotent replay, parent closure and concurrent-writer tests pass.'],['Authority','Strict or approved bounded remote-read contract implemented; no stale-epoch resurrection; fail closed on lost authority.'],['Performance','Per-operation/cell p95/p99 targets at agreed peak for 60 minutes; 24-hour normal soak; errors and load-generator drops included.'],['Recovery','AZ and authority loss tested; 30-minute receiver outage drains in ≤60 minutes at design incoming rate with revocation priority.'],['Operations','Signed runbooks, on-call drill, regional evidence, restore quarantine and controlled rollback.'],['Business release','Approved capped population, shadow reconciliation, 1% → 5% → 25% canary with hold points and named rollback owner.']]))+
'<div class="link-grid"><a href="'+lab+'#pilot"><span>PERSONAL CHECKLIST</span><h3>Track the actions →</h3><p>Browser-local ticks do not certify control completion.</p></a><a href="https://sovereign-data-monitor.paulcull.chatgpt.site/scale/pilot-actions.csv"><span>DOWNLOAD</span><h3>Action list CSV →</h3><p>Import owners, dependencies and exit gates into your delivery tooling.</p></a></div>',
scale_prompt+'Convert P01–P24 into a pilot backlog while preserving dependencies and exit evidence. Validate team capacity and environment availability before promising dates. Start with read-only shadow and capped approved population. Keep security, migration, HA and performance gates explicit. Stop rollout on any sovereignty leak, stale authorisation or material SLO breach; perform the rehearsed rollback. Do not treat simulated performance as pilot acceptance.',group='Deliver')
